ns through outside money: a Trump-linked super PAC has put about $8 million into ads attacking Suozzi over his stock trading, and Republican officials are working to consolidate the ticket in Nassau County. Suozzi has countered with a moderate record, bipartisan legislation, and explicit distance from his party's left wing. The fundamentals and the spending gap still point to a Democratic hold, with the attack campaign the main source of risk.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9133, "margin": 9.07}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.894, "margin": 8.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.8981, "margin": 8.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.907, "margin": 9.5}]}